                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Damiani appears fifteen times between 1802 and 1810 and is referred to in the 1796 list.  The meetings suggest that he is connected to 
      <persName key="JOH01">Johnson</persName> and to the British Museum. Godwin wrote to him with questions on Florentine history, specifically the Medicis,
     and for Italian translations.</p>
                        <p>A Damiani  wrote ‘A tribute to the memory of the late Rev. Mr. Joseph Robertson’, <title>Monthly Magazine</title>, 13 (1802), 133–7.</p>
                    </note>
